  "rationale": "Genome-wide MinLibCas9 knockout screens (37,686 guides, 2 per gene, no non-targeting guides) in two THP-1 IFNB1-GFP reporter clones (B6, C3; mapped to GEO 'IBER Clone 1' and 'Clone 2' by GSM order, not stated in GEO), each screened twice (repeats 1 and 2), stimulated with cGAMP either unprimed or after IFN-a priming and sorted into GFP-negative and GFP-high (top 5% for primed) populations. Column names match the GSM titles for condition and repeat. Positive regulators of IFNB1 induction (STING/TMEM173, TBK1, the paper's TBL1XR1 and HDAC3) are enriched in GFP-negative relative to GFP-high; negative regulators go the other way. Each GFP-negative library is paired with the GFP-high library sorted from the same culture (culture = clone x repeat), giving 8 libraries and 3 residual df per arm. Library totals. The library has no non-targeting guides, so control calibration and the control null are not available.",
